-- title:
--   From HTo GStage Mass Terminal Eq
-- statement:
--   **The terminal from-H-to-G stage is the Bernoulli-tail mass.**
--
--   Let `params` be LIDT parameters with a field model, let `psi_bi` be a quantum state on the two-register index set `ι × ι`, let `family` be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family, and let `k` be a natural number. At stage `k`, the remaining type has length zero, so the suffix sandwich is the identity and the recurrence has converted all `k` type bits into the Bernoulli-tail operator. The exact scalar identity is
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{fromHToGStageMass}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},k,k)
--   =
--   \operatorname{fromHToGBernoulliTailMass}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},k).
--   $$
--
--   This identifies the terminal endpoint of the stage recurrence and is used by `fromHToG_ofGHatFactsAndHalfSandwich` in the final comparison with the Bernoulli tail.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGStageMass_terminal_eq`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE/blob/f382c801026f53a9efc260fdee707cb35e0adb15/MIPStarRE/LDT/Pasting/Bernoulli/FromHToG/Core/StageMass.lean#L27-L50

